{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj8vAGejb1vMAkryahsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B2xstHuV35td2jr1MmQiGb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-982\\docs\\reviews\\wi-982\\003-ADJUDICATE-9973897.md","content":"Adjudicated: 997389725\n\n## amendment\n\nJudged on the cells as shown: LLR-360 `Detail` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:911e9b0c29295bd9) and TC-399 `Expected` and `Method` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:0ed55ebbe86913e9). The rung is released. To decide whether to bless the MEANING rows, I read the new text against the build: the WI-982 spec's Done-when, the mint (`intake._authoring_tags`, `_amendment_drafts`, `_first_approval_drafts`, `_draft_row`) and the reader (`hats.context_from_work_item`).\n\n- [MEANING] LLR-360 Detail -> before: a decomposition-round brief widens each parent need by \"the authoring work item's declared tags\", and says nothing about where a minted row's tags come from, so a minted row widened by its own Workstream and SafetyClass (`process`/`adjudication`) -> after: a merge-minted row RECORDS the declared tags of the work items its route names as authors; those recorded tags REPLACE the row's own classification when it is widened; a route naming no author records none, and the row widens by its own tags; a row minted from a minted row passes the record on; and the minted and in-lane sittings for one SR reach one perspective set wherever the author is named -> not the same. A correct build of the old text, where a minted row widens by `process`/`adjudication`, fails the new text, which adds a recording duty, a replacement rule, a pass-on rule and a cross-route equality. I would not bless the new text as written: \"A row the merge mints records the declared tags of the work items a route names as its authors\" covers EVERY merge-minted row. The build records the cell only on first-approval and amendment rows. Those two drafters are its only writers, and a `## Dispositions` draft that declares the cell is refused (`tests/test_intake.py::test_a_dispositions_block_may_not_declare_authoring_tags`). So a disposition or handback successor minted at the same merge, whose route names the same lane, records nothing, and the sentence is false of it. The WI-982 Done-when scopes the duty correctly (\"Every first-approval and amendment row minted by a route that names an authoring work item\"), and the LLR should state the same scope. Lesser, folded into the same fix: \"the merge mints\" leaves out the `sweep --merged ... --branch` route, which also records the cell (`test_a_merged_sweep_unions_the_named_rows_tags`), while the very next clause speaks of \"a route\". The row keeps its id: the amendment adds detail under the same SR-161 decision and leaves every approved sentence byte-exact, which is within §4 \"Keep or mint\". It is not re-anchored; see Dispositions.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-399 Expected, Method -> before: verify the round/non-round states, needs as parents, tag widening without sibling merge, the roster cases, the template slot, the combined sitting and non-ruling outcome lines -> after: the same states plus four: a minted row's recorded authoring tags stand in place of its own; a row minted from a minted row passes them on; the minted and in-lane rows for one SR compose one hat set; and a route naming no authoring work item leaves the row widening by its own tags. Expected now requires one perspective set across the two routes wherever the author is named -> not the same, because the TC now obliges four more checks and one more expected outcome. I would bless it as written. Each new clause is a reader-side or route-side behaviour the build has, and the coordinator's arms map binds each one to an existing evidence node in the row (`test_hats.py` for the replace and fall-back reads; `test_intake.py` for the slot mint on both row kinds, the merged-sweep union, the pass-on, the paired-shape equality, the branchless empty cell and the bare sweep). Unlike the LLR sentence, the method's \"a minted row's recorded authoring tags stand in place of its own\" states the reader's rule, which holds for every row whose cell is non-empty, so it is true as written. It names no carrier and keeps the existing clauses verbatim. Its new text needs no change when LLR-360's scope sentence is narrowed, so it can be re-attested now.\n\nThe rung is released, so neither row is held for the owner. The two rows sit in different registries, so LLR-360's plain MEANING holds no CLARITY row back: there is none in this sitting. The later act re-attests TC-399 only.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=2\n\n## Dispositions\n\n```toml\ntitle = \"LLR-360 amendment return: the authoring-tags sentence covers every merge-minted row, while only first-approval and amendment rows record the cell; narrow it to those two kinds and to the routes that mint them\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsafety_class = \"spine\"\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\npriority = 5\nspecref = \"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\"\nsr_refs = [\"SR-161\"]\nneeds = [\"WI-982\"]\n```\n\nVERDICT THIS CONTINUES: `docs/reviews/wi-982/003-ADJUDICATE-9973897.md`, `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`. LLR-360 is plain MEANING (not blessed) and TC-399 is MEANING+BLESS. The build is not in question. One cell, LLR-360 `detail`, and only its two added sentences:\n\n1. Restrict \"A row the merge mints records the declared tags of the work items a route names as its authors\" to the two kinds the build writes it on, a minted first-approval or amendment row, so that a disposition, handback or gap row minted at the same merge is no longer read as owing the record. The WI-982 Done-when wording is the model.\n2. In the same sentence, name the minting routes so that `sweep --merged ... --branch` is covered beside the merge slot. \"A first-approval or amendment row a route mints\" serves both and matches the following clause's \"a route\".\n\nEvery approved sentence of the cell stays byte-exact, and TC-399 needs no edit for this. Then re-sit the amendment. If WI-982's own lane makes this edit and its next amendment sitting blesses it before merge, this row has nothing left to do and closes on that record.\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3229,"cache_read_input_tokens":197889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3229},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c376c8c-200c-488f-950a-1fb2b7b7f425","uuid":"d2ab5e2f-f3a9-4497-81e1-715b527706d1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:19:00.749Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj8vA7jJCx52pYaKCyvm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01B2xstHuV35td2jr1MmQiGb":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-982\\docs\\reviews\\wi-982\\003-ADJUDICATE-9973897.md","content":"Adjudicated: 997389725\n\n## amendment\n\nJudged on the cells as shown: LLR-360 `Detail` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:911e9b0c29295bd9) and TC-399 `Expected` and `Method` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:0ed55ebbe86913e9). The rung is released. To decide whether to bless the MEANING rows, I read the new text against the build: the WI-982 spec's Done-when, the mint (`intake._authoring_tags`, `_amendment_drafts`, `_first_approval_drafts`, `_draft_row`) and the reader (`hats.context_from_work_item`).\n\n- [MEANING] LLR-360 Detail -> before: a decomposition-round brief widens each parent need by \"the authoring work item's declared tags\", and says nothing about where a minted row's tags come from, so a minted row widened by its own Workstream and SafetyClass (`process`/`adjudication`) -> after: a merge-minted row RECORDS the declared tags of the work items its route names as authors; those recorded tags REPLACE