{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj93hMNmYLZ2gks4pkp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both rows changed meaning, not just clarity. I blessed TC-399's new text and sent LLR-360 back. The verdict is committed as `a0be30f10` in `docs/reviews/wi-982/003-ADJUDICATE-9973897.md`. It ends with `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2` and `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`, and the commit carries the `WI: WI-982` and `Loop-Session` trailers.\n\n- **LLR-360 — meaning changed, not blessed.** The new sentences add real obligations: a minted row records its authors' tags, those tags replace the row's own classification, the record passes on to rows minted from it, and the two adjudication routes reach the same perspectives. A build that met the old text fails the new one. I can't bless it as written because \"A row the merge mints records…\" covers every minted row. In the code, only first-approval and amendment rows get the authoring-tags cell. A row minted from a `## Dispositions` block at the same merge records nothing, and a test confirms that. The WI-982 spec's Done-when already scopes it correctly to those two row kinds. The same sentence also says \"the merge\" but leaves out the `sweep --merged` route, which records the tags too.\n- **TC-399 — meaning changed, blessed.** It adds four checks and one expected outcome. Each new clause matches behaviour the code has, and each maps to an existing test in its evidence list. It needs no edit when LLR-360 is narrowed, so the later act can re-attest it now.\n\nThe verdict includes a `## Dispositions` draft, which the intake parser accepts. It asks for one edit to LLR-360's two new sentences: name first-approval and amendment rows, and say \"a route\" instead of \"the merge\". Every approved sentence stays byte-exact, then the amendment is re-judged. If the WI-982 lane makes that edit and a later sitting blesses it before merge, the draft has nothing left to do.\n\nI changed no registry cell. The `.requested` file is still untracked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3074,"cache_read_input_tokens":201118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3074},"output_tokens":668,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c376c8c-200c-488f-950a-1fb2b7b7f425","uuid":"1255987f-54ad-4ce9-9e55-6ebb79021b08","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:29.213Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj93h3Gv835j3qwjrcnE"}
